            {
              "id": "neetprep_physics_q450886",
              "type": "mcq",
              "originalOrder": 6,
              "topic": "Thermal Expansion",
              "subtopic": "Thermal Expansion",
              "sub_category": "Thermal Expansion",
              "chapter": "Thermal Properties of Matter",
              "exam_name": "NCERT Based",
              "question": "The radius of a metal sphere at room temperature <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(T\\)</span> is <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(R,\\)</span>&nbsp;and the coefficient of linear expansion of the metal is <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\alpha.\\)</span>&nbsp;The sphere is heated a little by a temperature <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\Delta T\\)</span> so that its new temperature is&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(T + \\Delta T.\\)</span>&nbsp;The increase in the volume of the sphere is approximately:<br>1.&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(2 \\pi R \\alpha \\Delta T \\)</span><br>2.&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\pi R^2 \\alpha \\Delta T \\)</span><br>3.&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(4 \\pi R^3 \\alpha \\Delta T / 3 \\)</span><br>4.&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(4 \\pi R^3 \\alpha \\Delta T\\)</span>",
              "options": [
                "(1)",
                "(2)",
                "(3)",
                "(4)"
              ],
              "correct": 3,
              "explanation": "Hint: There will be a volumetric expansion in the sphere.\n\nStep 1: Find the volume of the sphere.\nLet the radius of the sphere be \\(R.\\) As the temperature increases, the volume\nincreases as shown in the figure.\nThe original volume is given by;\n\\(V_o=\\frac{4}{3}πR^3\\)\n\n\nStep 2: Find the increase in the volume of the sphere.\nThe coefficient of linear expansion \\(= α\\)\nThe coefficient of volume expansion \\(= 3α\\)\n\\(\\frac{1}{V} \\frac{d V}{d T}=3 \\alpha\\)\n\\( \\Rightarrow d V=3 V \\alpha d t \\simeq 4 \\pi {R}^3 \\alpha \\Delta {T}\\)\nHence, option (4) is the correct answer.<div style=\"margin-top:1.25rem; padding:0.85rem 1rem; background:var(--bg-secondary); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px;\"><div style=\"display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; margin-bottom:0.6rem; font-weight:600; font-size:0.88rem;\"><span>📊 Student Attempt Analytics</span><span style=\"padding:2px 8px; border-radius:12px; font-size:0.75rem; font-weight:700; background:rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.15); color:#16a34a;\">🟢 Easy · 72% Got This Correct</span></div><div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:0.5rem; text-align:center; font-size:0.82rem;\"><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);\"><div>(1)</div><div style=\"font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;\">4%</div></div><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);\"><div>(2)</div><div style=\"font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;\">5%</div></div><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);\"><div>(3)</div><div style=\"font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;\">20%</div></div><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:rgba(34,197,94,0.12); border:1.5px solid #22c55e;\"><div style=\"color:#16a34a; font-weight:700;\">(4) ✓</div><div style=\"font-weight:800; color:#16a34a; margin-top:2px;\">73%</div></div></div></div>",
              "ncert": true
