        {
          "topic": "Radiation",
          "questions": [
            {
              "id": "neetprep_physics_q450887",
              "type": "mcq",
              "originalOrder": 7,
              "topic": "Radiation",
              "subtopic": "Radiation",
              "sub_category": "Radiation",
              "chapter": "Thermal Properties of Matter",
              "exam_name": "NCERT Based",
              "question": "A sphere, a cube, and a thin circular plate, all of the same material and the same mass are initially heated to the same high temperature. Then:\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>the plate will cool fastest and the cube the slowest</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>the sphere will cool fastest and the cube the slowest</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td>the plate will cool fastest and the sphere the slowest</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td>cube will cool fastest and plate the slowest.</td></tr></tbody></table>",
              "options": [
                "(1)",
                "(2)",
                "(3)",
                "(4)"
              ],
              "correct": 2,
              "explanation": "Hint:The rate of cooling depends on the surface area of the body.\nStep: Find the rate of cooling for three bodies in terms of surface area.\nConsider the diagram where all three objects are heated to the same temperature \n\\(T.\\)We know that density,\\(\\rho=\\frac{\\text{mass}}{\\text{volume}}\\)is the same\nfor all three objects. Hence, the volume will also be the same.\nThe rate of cooling of an object depends on its surface area relative to its\nvolume because heat is lost through the surface. For objects of the same mass\nand material, the object with the largest surface area will cool fastest.\nAccording to Stefan’s law of heat loss,\n\\(\\frac{dQ}{dt}=\\sigma eAT^4\\)\nwe know that\\(A\\) is the surface area of for object and \\(T\\) is the\ntemperature.\nAs the plate's thickness is the least, the surface area of the plate is maximum.\nHence,\\(𝐻 _{𝑠phere} : 𝐻_{cube}: 𝐻_{plate} = 𝐴_{𝑠phere} : 𝐴_{cube} :\nA_{plate}\\)As\\(𝐴 _{𝑝late}\\)is maximum, the plate will cool faster.\nA thin plate has a large surface area relative to its volume, so it will cool\nthe fastest.\nA sphere has the smallest surface area for a given volume, so it will cool the\nslowest.\nThe cube falls in between the plate and the sphere in terms of surface area to\nvolume ratio.\nThus, the plate will cool the fastest and the sphere the slowest.\nHence, option (3) is the correct answer.<div style=\"margin-top:1.25rem; padding:0.85rem 1rem; background:var(--bg-secondary); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px;\"><div style=\"display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; margin-bottom:0.6rem; font-weight:600; font-size:0.88rem;\"><span>📊 Student Attempt Analytics</span><span style=\"padding:2px 8px; border-radius:12px; font-size:0.75rem; font-weight:700; background:rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.15); color:#d97706;\">🟡 Medium · 57% Got This Correct</span></div><div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:0.5rem; text-align:center; font-size:0.82rem;\"><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);\"><div>(1)</div><div style=\"font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;\">15%</div></div><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);\"><div>(2)</div><div style=\"font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;\">20%</div></div><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:rgba(34,197,94,0.12); border:1.5px solid #22c55e;\"><div style=\"color:#16a34a; font-weight:700;\">(3) ✓</div><div style=\"font-weight:800; color:#16a34a; margin-top:2px;\">58%</div></div><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);\"><div>(4)</div><div style=\"font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;\">10%</div></div></div></div>",
